<title>POLAND: Budimex 1996 payout unlikely - official.</title>
<headline>Budimex 1996 payout unlikely - official.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction company Budimex SA is unlikely to pay a 1996 dividend because it had to invest heavily in its group's expansion, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The management's initial assessment and...investments in the holding's expansion and strengthening justify a proposal to pass the dividend,&quot; company president's adviser Eugeniusz Trajer told Reuters.</p>
<p>He added, however, that the issue was still under consideration and the final decision would be announced in the end of April.</p>
<p>Last year Budimex had a net profit of 18.6 million zlotys on 272.4-million-zloty-sales and it invested 39 million zlotys.</p>
<p>Budimex did not pay a dividend for 1995.</p>
<p>-- Malgorzata Rzepka +48 22 653 9700</p>
